 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport bisect\n\ndef fckset(arr, m):\n    n = len(arr)\n    halfsum = []\n    mx = 1 << n\n    \n    for i in range(mx):\n        hlf = 0\n        for j in range(n):\n            if (i >> j) & 1:\n                hlf = (hlf + arr[j]) % m\n        halfsum.append(hlf)\n    \n    return halfsum\n\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\narr = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Handle edge case where array is empty\nif n == 0:\n    print(0)\n    exit()\n\n# Split array into two halves\nmid = n // 2\nh1 = fckset(arr[:mid], m)\nh2 = fckset(arr[mid:], m)\n\nh2.sort()\n\nresult = 0\nfor i in h1:\n    # We want to find the largest j in h2 such that (i + j) % m is maximized\n    # This is equivalent to finding j such that i + j < m (if possible) or i + j >= m\n    # The maximum value of (i + j) % m is either i + j (if i + j < m) or i + j - m (if i + j >= m)\n    # To maximize (i + j) % m, we want to maximize either i + j (if < m) or i + j - m (if >= m)\n    # For i + j < m, we want j < m - i\n    # For i + j >= m, we want j as small as possible (since i + j - m is maximized when j is minimized)\n    \n    # First, try to find the largest j such that j <= m - i - 1\n    idx = bisect.bisect_left(h2, m - i) - 1\n    if idx >= 0:\n        result = max(result, (i + h2[idx]) % m)\n    \n    # Also consider the smallest element in h2 (for the case where i + j >= m)\n    if h2:\n        result = max(result, (i + h2[0]) % m)\n\nprint(result)\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.7\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.622600959512056e-06, -4.136476854910143e-05, -1.4305104514278355e-06, 0.0, -1.7046782886609435e-05, -0.0002768848498817533, -4.291525328881107e-06, -5.8410845667822286e-05, -0.0011831672163680196, -0.06263216584920883, -4.792098479811102e-05, -4.172316494077677e-06, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -0.048589371144771576, -1.9907753085135482e-05, -3.433168603805825e-05, -1.19